course: dictionary
lesson: 14564
title: Words about the body
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you about a person's body. Physique is one of them. It means the size and shape of a body, especially how strong and muscly it is. «The goalkeeper had a tall, strong physique.» The words tall and strong are the clues: they tell you what kind of body is meant.
explain: Look at the words around it to work out its meaning. «The swimmer had a slim physique, built for speed through the water.» Slim and built for speed show that physique describes the shape and build of the body. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Body shape fits, so physique must mean body build.
explain: Physique is a noun, so it names a thing. Different people have different physiques. Health lessons teach that every body is different and that being healthy matters more than having any particular physique.
fact: Physique means the size and shape of a person's body.
fact: Physique often means how strong or muscly a body is.
fact: «The rugby player had a powerful physique.» Powerful means strong.
fact: «Her slim physique suited ballet.» Slim means thin in a neat, narrow way.
fact: Every body is different, and being healthy matters more than having any particular physique.
exercise: «The weightlifter had a massive, muscly physique.» What does physique mean here? | A sad face | The name of his gym | The kind of shoes he wore | *The size and shape of his body
exercise: Which word in «The coach said every physique is different.» means not the same? | *different | said | every | coach
exercise: A health lesson teaches that every body is different. What is the main message? | Physique is another word for a name | Everyone must have the same physique | *Being healthy matters more than having one particular physique | Only tall people can be healthy
test: «He had a tall, slim physique that suited running.» What does physique mean? | A type of running shoe | *Body size and shape | A loud shout | A kind of football
test: What does «muscly» tell you about a physique? | It is hard to see | *It has strong, well-developed muscles | It is very small | It makes a noise
exam: «Health lessons teach that being healthy matters more than a certain physique.» What is the main message? | Everyone must train until they look the same | Only strong physiques are worth having | *Being healthy is more important than having any one kind of body | Physique does not exist
